<title>TURKEY: Turk Is Bankasi 96 net profits triple.</title>
<headline>Turk Is Bankasi 96 net profits triple.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Dec 1996 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)     3,803.62   vs   1,203.80</p>
<p>    Net profit		     38,036.21   vs  12,038.04</p>
<p>    Net interest income	  72,187.40   vs  34,607.46</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense   14,566.93   vs  16,068.94</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans    6,210.19   vs     644.05</p>
<p>    Loans			   314,508.78   vs 138,287.31</p>
<p>    Deposits			474,904.95   vs 247,460.35</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed		 57,331.94   vs  20,836.03</p>
<p>    Equity			   48,627.59   vs  28,993.21</p>
<p>    Capital			  10,000.00   vs  10,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - T.Is bankasi A.S. is one of Turkey's biggest commercial banks.</p>
<p>For each 1,000 lira nominal-valued share, the bank plans to pay out a 24,680 lira dividend for A series, 1,203 lira for B series, 400.5 lira for C series and 16.9 million lira per founder share from April 30 after approval at the annual meeting of shareholders and directors on March 31.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into consideration Turkey's 84.9 percent 1996 wholesale inflation.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
